//   1 FALSE EVIDENCE. A sample the facing gate never traced (vis 0, no ray) was noted BLOCKED, and so was
//     a ray stopped by the receiver's own surface right at P (the terminator / self-shadow on a smooth
//     curved low-poly surface -- exactly the face / cylinder / snow cases). Neither says anything about a
//     light behind a wall. Now only a TRACED sample is evidence, and a blocked one only when its opaque
//     caster lies at least the patch edge (OCC_BLOCK_MIN .. OCC_BLOCK_MAX) away (occEvidence): local geometry a patch-
//     wide verdict cannot represent never culls. (VIS hands the verdict to SHADE in pdnVisPack's bit 30.)
//   2 TOO LITTLE EVIDENCE. The count is in FRAMES with at least one blocked ray, and a rest light gets
