#ifdef CLEAN_VIS_QUEUE
// (#1039 M1) THE PRODUCER: entry dest's sun / moon ray as rtShadeHit would trace it at the hit of the RT LIT
// RECORD r0..r3 -- read back exactly as the lighting stage reads it (rtLitUnpack: the same rounding, the
// same footprint), seen from eye (the receiver), its want test (water: the glint above 1e-4; fullbright:
// none; else N.L > 0) and its set-up (rtHitSunRay: the escape check, the back-face self-shadow, the
// origin) -- queued as one VQ_K_SUN request (the walk kernel runs rtSunRayVis with the same switches), or a
// constant result where no ray is cast. inCap false (an entry past the queue's capacity): nothing -- the
// fused lighting stage's tail shades that entry. Every active lane calls it once (the append's ballot).
// (#1039 M2, -DCLEAN_VIS_QUEUE_M2) + the hit's other rays, in rtShadeHit's order (each with the alpha-test
// cone the inline walk would see: a traced sun ray leaves it at the hit's footprint, spread 0 --
// rtHitSunShadowCore -- for every later ray of the hit):
//   * the RT reflections' OCCLUSION ray (rtrHitEnv: rtrOccRay along the reflection direction rtShadeHit asks
//     the environment for -- the water's wave reflection, else reflect(-V, N) --, from the arrival side
//     g_rtr_hit_ng of the record's Ng; Rin = the reflection ray's direction): one VQ_K_OCC request;
//   * the LOCAL LIGHTS: rtHitLocalLights on the record with RT_SHADE_BUDGET_OUT (the same walk the lighting
//     stage ran: the light grid's picks, the cluster, every BRDF -- every share unshadowed) -> that sum into
//     the SUM slot, and the hit shadow-ray budget's picks as VQ_K_LIGHT requests (rtrProjRaySetup; the share
//     in the pick's slot, the walk leaves the blocked part there);
//   * the BLEND LAYERS' cone flag into the layer slot (the RT split's LAYERS stage reads it).
// hit false (M2's RT REQ runs every entry: a miss / a back-face stop has no material): only the layer flag.
#if VQ_PRODUCER_STAGE
void vqHitRequests(uvec4 r0, uvec4 r1, uvec4 r2, uvec4 r3, vec3 eye, vec3 Rin, uint e, bool inCap, bool hit)
{
    VqRegion r = vqRegion();
    const uint db = vqDest(r, e, 0u);   // (entry e's slot 0)
    bool want = false;
    vec3 Po = vec3(0.0);
    const vec3 L = atmosLightDir();
    float tmax = 0.0;
    uint wanted = 0u, consts = 0u;
    const bool shade = inCap && hit;
    const RtLitSurface s = rtLitUnpack(r0, r1, r2, r3);   // (sets rt_surf_foot: the casters' LOD; zeros for no hit)
    const bool water = s.model == RT_SURF_WATER;
