// alpha-blend / water layer's reflection -> uRtFwd (rgb, a = its view depth; 0 = none) ----
// THE WAVES (#1020): the TLAS holds the flat LL water planes; a water hit moves onto the displaced
// sea surface along the ray (seaRayHit) before its reflection and its depth -- so the water FS's
// depth match (rtFwdIn) holds on a crest -- and reflects off the waves' slope.
// (#1493) THE WATER RECEIVER'S REFLECTION RAY NEVER SEES THE WATER CLASS: the flat plane in the TLAS
// is a stand-in for the very surface the ray leaves, not something in its reflection. From a trough
// (the displaced point below the flat plane) the upward R (rtWaterReflectDir: R.z >= 0) met that
// plane from underneath a few cm / dm away; the hit shaded as water seen from below (rtShadeHit's
// eye = the receiver, under the plane: the water fog colour) and the water FS spliced it -- dark
// blotches over every trough, the sky only on the crests: the camouflage pattern of the Gerstner
// sum's sign, at the half-resolution block grid. A crest's ray (above the plane, upward) never met it.
// Glass and other blend receivers keep the water class (a window over the sea reflects the sea).
#include "clean_sea_state.glsl"
// The ray o + t dir from the flat water hit (tFlat) onto the displaced surface: a fixed-point march
// over the height under the point (the horizontal shift inverted one step a pass), bounded to the
// waves' height band. x0: the undisplaced sea point found.
// (#1493) The surface is the DRAWN one: the waves VS (clean_water_waves.vert seaPoint) fades each
// wave's geometry by the camera's horizontal distance to the undisplaced point; the march takes the
// same fade (camDist), so the far field's point -- the reflection's origin and the depth rtFwdIn
// matches -- is where the raster put the water, not a full-amplitude trough under a flat drawn sea.
vec3 seaRayHit(vec3 o, vec3 dir, float tFlat, out vec2 x0)
{
    const float dz = abs(dir.z) > 1e-3 ? dir.z : (dir.z < 0.0 ? -1e-3 : 1e-3);
    const float band = (2.0 * seaHs() + ssr.sea[2].y + 1.0) / abs(dz);
    float t = tFlat;
    vec2 xy = o.xy + dir.xy * t;
    x0 = xy;
    [[unroll]] for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
    {
        const SeaSurf ss = seaSurface(x0, length(x0 - ssr.cam_origin.xy), 0.0);
        const float zt = waterHeight() + ss.dh + ss.disp.z;
        t = clamp((zt - o.z) / dz, tFlat - band, tFlat + band);
        xy = o.xy + dir.xy * t;
        x0 = xy - ss.disp.xy;
