// THE LAYER'S LIGHT (RenderVKBlendFrontLight; clean_surface_light.glsl blendFrontIn): the visibility terms the front
// blend layer's own lighting (RenderVKBlendHitLighting) traced per fragment and per frame -- up to ~10 rays per
// layer, with no history -- here once per half-resolution texel and resolved over frames like its GI (rows [10 h,
// 15 h), clean_rt_fwd_temporal.h):
//   r  the sun / moon visibility: one ray, the RT reflection hits' rule (rtHitSunShadow; its tint is not kept);
//   g  its local lights' SHADOWED / UNSHADOWED ratio: the hit estimator (rtHitLocalLights, the RT reflection hits'
//      budget) twice over the SAME picks -- the same seed and stratum -- once with its shadow rays and once with every
//      visibility 1 (g_rtr_novis): the ratio of Heitz et al. 2018. The FS keeps its own per-pixel, normal-mapped,
//      specular local light (its unshadowed forward walk) and takes only the shadowing from here. The ratio's surface:
//      a white diffuse legacy one at the layer's point and viewer-side normal;
//   b  the occlusion ray along the mirror direction of its smooth normal (blendHitOcc's: GI frames only, else 1);
//   a  the layer's alpha (the deeper layers' visible weight: clean_surface_light.glsl blendFrontBudget).
vec4 rfvLight(RtSurface ls, float hdist, vec3 dir, vec3 nf, vec3 ngf, float pa)
{
    const vec3 P = ls.P;
    const vec3 V = -dir;
    float sv = 1.0;
    const vec3 Ls = atmosLightDir();
    if (dot(nf, Ls) > 0.0)
